  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.co.try": "Turn off \"Code checks for cancellation\" and cancel during unit 2: does the coroutine stop?",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.co.request": "In Kotlin, coroutine cancellation is cooperative: coroutines react to cancellation only when they suspend or check for cancellation explicitly. [[src:kt-cancellation]]",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.co.swallow": "Swallowing `CancellationException` defeats cancellation at that spot. [[badge:guideline]]",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.co.noswallow": "To enable cancellation, do not consume exceptions of type `CancellationException`: do not catch them, or always rethrow them when caught. Prefer catching specific types such as `IOException` over `Exception` or `Throwable`. [[src:and-co-best]]",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.co.cleanupPlain": "It is easy to assume `finally` will finish its cleanup. For suspending cleanup, without `NonCancellable` it gets cancelled.",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.co.cleanupNC": "Pass `NonCancellable` only to `withContext`, and use it for cleanup that must run. Avoid it with `launch` or `async` because it breaks structured concurrency. [[src:kt-cancellation]]",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.co.timeout": "`withTimeoutOrNull` fits when you want a fallback (for example the local cache) instead of handling an exception. Both rely on cooperative cancellation. [[src:kt-cancellation]]",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.co.nocoop": "Neither cancel nor timeout can stop non-cooperative code at once: in this example the coroutine ran to the last unit despite the request to stop.",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.sk.stop.what": "Stopping at the check",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.sk.stop.why": "the cancellation exception was swallowed, or there is no check",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.sk.cleanup.what": "The suspending cleanup in finally",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.sk.cleanup.why": "the Job is cancelled and the cleanup is not inside NonCancellable",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.ch.cancelling": "Job: active → cancelling",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.ch.stopSkipped": "The request to stop is ignored here",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.ch.stopped": "The coroutine stops at the check",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.ch.endCancelled": "Job: cancelling → cancelled",
