  "track.coroutines.m.exception.title": "Exceptions and supervision",
  "track.coroutines.m.exception.overview": "A scope has two child coroutines and one of them throws. You choose `launch` or `async`, `coroutineScope` or `supervisorScope`, where to put a `CoroutineExceptionHandler` and how to catch, and see where the failure ends up.",
  "track.coroutines.m.exception.wrapup": "The path of a failure depends on the builder and the scope kind. With `coroutineScope` a child failure goes up to the parent. A `CoroutineExceptionHandler` receives the unhandled errors of the root coroutine and its children, and it cannot recover: the coroutine has already completed when the handler runs.",
  "track.coroutines.m.exception.simp.1": "The rules are written as one pure function citing the documentation, simplified; cases with several simultaneous failures (suppressed exceptions) are not simulated. [[src:kt-exceptions]]",
  "track.coroutines.m.exception.simp.2": "\"Handler at the root\" means placed in the scope context so the children inherit it; this is a compact wording, not a list of every way to install a handler.",
  "track.coroutines.m.exception.ctl.hint": "Change each choice; the scenario and its steps are recomputed.",
