  "track.coroutines.m.flowpipe.title": "A Flow pipeline: buffer, conflate, collectLatest",
  "track.coroutines.m.flowpipe.overview": "The producer emits 5 values 100 ms apart (assumed); the collector takes 250 ms to process each. You choose how to connect the two and watch the timing and which values are dropped or cancelled.",
  "track.coroutines.m.flowpipe.wrapup": "By default the producer and the collector run sequentially, so a slow collector slows the producer. `buffer` lets the producer run ahead, `conflate` drops old values to keep the newest, and `collectLatest` cancels in-progress work when a new value arrives.",
  "track.coroutines.m.flowpipe.simp.1": "The timing numbers are assumptions; `map` only multiplies by 10 and takes no time. The real scheduler, `flowOn` and other operators are not simulated.",
