  "track.coroutines.m.lifecycle.co.repeat": "`repeatOnLifecycle(STARTED)` launches the block in a new coroutine every time the lifecycle is STARTED or above and cancels it when STOPPED. [[src:and-stateflow]]",
  "track.coroutines.m.lifecycle.co.waste": "Collecting a Flow while the screen is hidden can waste resources: values are received that nobody sees. In Compose, `collectAsStateWithLifecycle()` handles this by collecting in a lifecycle-aware way. [[src:and-state]]",
  "track.coroutines.m.lifecycle.co.finish": "Every ViewModel has a `viewModelScope`; a coroutine launched in it is cancelled automatically when the ViewModel is cleared. [[src:and-co-lifecycle]]",
  "track.coroutines.m.effects.title": "LaunchedEffect and rememberCoroutineScope",
  "track.coroutines.m.effects.overview": "A composable uses `LaunchedEffect(key)` to run a coroutine tied to the Composition and `rememberCoroutineScope` to run a coroutine from a tap. You recompose, change the key, tap the button, or let the composable leave the screen.",
  "track.coroutines.m.effects.wrapup": "A `LaunchedEffect` coroutine is cancelled when the composable leaves the Composition; if the key changes, the old coroutine is cancelled and a new one is launched; recomposing with the same key does not restart it. A coroutine from `rememberCoroutineScope` is also cancelled when the composable leaves the Composition.",
  "track.coroutines.m.effects.simp.1": "The recomposition mechanism, `rememberUpdatedState` and the other effects are not simulated; a recompose is simply an event that keeps the key.",
